1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:04,305
SYMBIOTIC CITY — self-healing urban intelligence, built for the World Problem Solver

2
00:00:04,355 --> 00:00:08,009
track. This is the full platform walkthrough.

3
00:00:10,509 --> 00:00:15,223
Aurora Vale is a synthetic city. Infrastructure fails in chains — one trip cascades

4
00:00:15,273 --> 00:00:19,986
into hospitals, water supply, and thousands of residents. This platform answers two

5
00:00:20,036 --> 00:00:24,749
questions: how far does a failure spread, and what do we fix first?

6
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:29,849
Every screen behind this wall is role-protected. We sign in as the City Operator —

7
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:33,550
one of four roles with server-enforced permissions.

8
00:00:35,919 --> 00:00:39,563
The dashboard is the live command surface: city health index, zone status, active

9
00:00:39,613 --> 00:00:43,256
incidents and recovery progress. Every number is served from the platform database —

10
00:00:43,306 --> 00:00:46,949
nothing on this screen is mocked.

11
00:00:49,139 --> 00:00:53,262
The digital twin renders all twenty-three assets and twenty-five dependency links as

12
00:00:53,312 --> 00:00:57,434
a live 3-D scene. Camera presets frame the whole city — isometric, top-down,

13
00:00:57,484 --> 00:01:01,607
perspective — and dragging orbits around the model. Colour is live status: mint

14
00:01:01,657 --> 00:01:05,780
operational, amber degraded, coral failed.

15
00:01:10,089 --> 00:01:14,063
We select the Aurora Vale Generating Station. The panel opens with capacity, zone,

16
00:01:14,113 --> 00:01:18,086
criticality rank, and its dependency fan-out — the upstream feeders, and every

17
00:01:18,136 --> 00:01:22,109
downstream customer that relies on it.

18
00:01:26,589 --> 00:01:30,779
This dependency graph is the foundation of everything else: simulation,

19
00:01:30,829 --> 00:01:35,019
optimization, and the recovery workflow all read the same model you are looking at.

20
00:01:41,089 --> 00:01:44,039
And the scene reports its own cost — meshes, draw calls, frames per second.

21
00:01:44,089 --> 00:01:47,039
Measured, not claimed.

22
00:01:49,489 --> 00:01:54,000
The assets live as data in the infrastructure registry — searchable, filterable,

23
00:01:54,049 --> 00:01:58,560
with zones, priorities and dependency links. Every change is audited.

24
00:02:00,009 --> 00:02:03,931
The City Copilot answers operational questions in plain language. We ask which

25
00:02:03,981 --> 00:02:07,903
assets are most critical in Aurora Vale. The reply is grounded and labelled — this

26
00:02:07,953 --> 00:02:11,875
one comes from the deterministic rule engine, with cited entities you can open. With

27
00:02:11,925 --> 00:02:15,847
a Groq key configured, the same panel upgrades to LLM responses; without one, it

28
00:02:15,897 --> 00:02:19,819
never pretends to be one.

29
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:26,467
The AI Disaster Commander turns the panel into an incident coordinator. If the

30
00:02:26,518 --> 00:02:30,715
generating station fails, what is affected, and what do we prioritize? The commander

31
00:02:30,766 --> 00:02:34,963
runs the real cascade engine and a CP-SAT preview: twelve failed assets, eighteen

32
00:02:35,014 --> 00:02:39,211
thousand residents at risk, prioritized actions — linked into simulation,

33
00:02:39,262 --> 00:02:43,459
optimization, and the twin.

34
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:49,207
Multi-scenario comparison runs two failure hypotheses side by side through the same

35
00:02:49,257 --> 00:02:53,415
deterministic cascade maths — one column per scenario: population, assets failed,

36
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:57,622
depth, severity — plus a plain-language trade-off. Every number is computed; the

37
00:02:57,672 --> 00:03:01,830
model only narrates.

38
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:07,282
The Failure Simulation Lab is where operators rehearse disasters. We inject a fault

39
00:03:07,332 --> 00:03:11,335
at the generating station and its substation, then run the cascade: breadth-first

40
00:03:11,384 --> 00:03:15,387
over the dependency graph, each asset scored against its redundancy envelope —

41
00:03:15,437 --> 00:03:19,439
deterministic, seeded, reproducible.

42
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,742
Simulation becomes accountability in incident management. We file a high-severity

43
00:03:24,792 --> 00:03:28,645
incident against a water-treatment asset. The backend enforces one open incident per

44
00:03:28,695 --> 00:03:32,547
asset and category, validates every transition, and records the full lifecycle from

45
00:03:32,597 --> 00:03:36,450
report to resolution.

46
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:42,659
Now the core of advanced challenge A02 — intelligent decisions and optimization. We

47
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:47,280
add demand for the failed asset and let OR-Tools CP-SAT allocate it: variables are

48
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:51,900
reservation quantities; constraints cover capacity, mobilisation and all-or-nothing

49
00:03:51,949 --> 00:03:56,519
service per asset; priorities drive the objective — maximize critical coverage. The

50
00:03:56,569 --> 00:04:01,139
solver returns an explained allocation with its objective value and proven status —

51
00:04:01,189 --> 00:04:05,759
or proves the problem infeasible.

52
00:04:06,739 --> 00:04:10,089
It never guesses — and nothing is approved until a human decides.

53
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:15,865
Every plan ships with explainable recovery intelligence: why each assignment was

54
00:04:15,915 --> 00:04:20,199
made, what was limiting, and alternatives the solver proved feasible.

55
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:26,510
Resource management is the allocator's inventory: crews, equipment and materials

56
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:31,420
with statuses, home zones and costs — the records CP-SAT drew from.

57
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:36,665
Dispatch turns approved plans into repair tasks, with object-level authorization —

58
00:04:36,715 --> 00:04:40,510
an engineer sees only the tasks assigned to them.

59
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:46,724
Advanced challenge A07 — automated multi-step workflow. For the incident we reported

60
00:04:46,774 --> 00:04:51,538
earlier, we start a real recovery workflow: the engine runs the automatic steps —

61
00:04:51,588 --> 00:04:56,352
record, validate, cascade simulation, constrained planning — then stops at the human

62
00:04:56,402 --> 00:05:01,166
approval gate. Validated transitions, idempotent retries, compensation for failures,

63
00:05:01,216 --> 00:05:05,980
and an append-only ledger for every step.

64
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:13,370
The resilience report summarizes structural risk from live records — dependency

65
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:18,360
hotspots, redundancy gaps, zone exposure. Computed by the platform, never invented.

66
00:05:19,810 --> 00:05:24,094
Analytics completes the loop with response times, task throughput and utilisation

67
00:05:24,144 --> 00:05:28,429
trends — measured from stored records, exportable for reporting.

68
00:05:29,879 --> 00:05:32,034
Notifications keep every role informed as incidents escalate and recoveries

69
00:05:32,084 --> 00:05:34,239
complete.

70
00:05:35,689 --> 00:05:40,134
Administration closes the loop: user management, the role and permission matrix, and

71
00:05:40,185 --> 00:05:44,629
an append-only audit log — who did what, when, with what outcome.

72
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:49,864
The platform documents its own model assumptions and limits. Aurora Vale is

73
00:05:49,914 --> 00:05:53,699
synthetic — and the product says so, everywhere it matters.

74
00:05:55,149 --> 00:06:00,114
SYMBIOTIC CITY brings deterministic simulation, CP-SAT optimization and grounded AI

75
00:06:00,164 --> 00:06:05,129
into one audited decision loop — humans approve every consequential action,

76
00:06:05,179 --> 00:06:10,144
role-based access is enforced server-side, and every result is reproducible from the

77
00:06:10,194 --> 00:06:15,159
seeded dataset. Infrastructure fails in chains. Recovery should be planned that way.

